IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-part2-prisoners`

-- Tests for regulations 2 and 3 (spr-part2-prisoners.l4).
-- Expected values are decided from the text of the regulation named beside each
-- group, before running.

§ `Fixtures`

-- A person who is in Great Britain and in none of the kinds of custody.
`a free person in Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

`imprisoned in Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

-- Imprisoned abroad, where the same circumstances in Great Britain would not make a prisoner.
`imprisoned abroad, not a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS FALSE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS TRUE

-- Imprisoned abroad, where the same circumstances in Great Britain would make a prisoner.
`imprisoned abroad, a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS FALSE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

`unlawfully at large abroad, not a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS FALSE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS TRUE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS TRUE

`unlawfully at large in Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS TRUE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

`detained under section 47, no release date certified` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS TRUE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

`detained under section 47, release date certified as 10 June 2026` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS TRUE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

`detained under section 47 but outside Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS FALSE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS TRUE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

`detained under section 136 in Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS TRUE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

`detained under section 136 but outside Great Britain` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS FALSE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS FALSE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS TRUE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE

-- A person in Great Britain who is imprisoned, with the "similar circumstances" flag set
-- anyway: paragraph (3) is about a person OUTSIDE Great Britain, so it must not apply.
`imprisoned in Great Britain with the similar-circumstances flag set` MEANS Custody WITH
    `the person is in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `the person is imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings` IS TRUE
    `the person is a prisoner who is unlawfully at large` IS FALSE
    `the person is detained under section 47 of the Mental Health Act 1983` IS FALSE
    `the release date that the Secretary of State has certified, if any` IS NOTHING
    `the person is detained under section 136 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) (Scotland) Act 2003` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS TRUE

`a day in the test period` MEANS YMD 2026 6 1

§ `Regulation 2(2): who is a prisoner`

-- (2)(a): imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with criminal proceedings,
-- in Great Britain: a prisoner.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `imprisoned in Great Britain`
-- A person in none of the kinds of custody is not a prisoner.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `a free person in Great Britain`)
-- (2)(a) "in Great Britain or elsewhere": imprisoned abroad where the same would make a prisoner in Great Britain.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `imprisoned abroad, a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain`
-- (2)(b): a prisoner unlawfully at large, in Great Britain.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `unlawfully at large in Great Britain`

-- (2)(c): in Great Britain, detained under section 47 of the 1983 Act, on or before the
-- certified release date. With release date 10 June 2026: 9 June and 10 June are within,
-- 11 June is not.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` (YMD 2026 6 9) `detained under section 47, release date certified as 10 June 2026`
#ASSERT `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` (YMD 2026 6 10) `detained under section 47, release date certified as 10 June 2026`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` (YMD 2026 6 11) `detained under section 47, release date certified as 10 June 2026`)
-- (2)(c)(ii) "(if any)": no certified release date, read as no day to be after (fork F5). Asserted.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` (YMD 2030 1 1) `detained under section 47, no release date certified`
-- (2)(c) is for a prisoner "in Great Britain": outside Great Britain it does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `detained under section 47 but outside Great Britain`)

-- (2)(d): in Great Britain, detained under section 136 of the Scottish Act 2003.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `detained under section 136 in Great Britain`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `detained under section 136 but outside Great Britain`)

§ `Regulation 2(3): outside Great Britain`

-- Imprisoned abroad and, in similar circumstances in Great Britain, not a prisoner:
-- not a prisoner within (2)(a).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `imprisoned abroad, not a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain`)
-- Unlawfully at large abroad, same: not a prisoner within (2)(b).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `unlawfully at large abroad, not a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain`)
-- Paragraph (3) is about a person outside Great Britain: in Great Britain the flag is irrelevant.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(2): the person is a prisoner mentioned in regulation 2(2) on the day` `a day in the test period` `imprisoned in Great Britain with the similar-circumstances flag set`
#ASSERT `regulation 2(3): the person is outside Great Britain and would not have been a prisoner there` `imprisoned abroad, not a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(3): the person is outside Great Britain and would not have been a prisoner there` `imprisoned abroad, a prisoner in similar circumstances in Great Britain`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(3): the person is outside Great Britain and would not have been a prisoner there` `imprisoned in Great Britain with the similar-circumstances flag set`)

§ `Regulation 3: persons remanded in custody`

`a custodial sentence imposed in Great Britain` MEANS Sentence WITH
    `the kind of sentence` IS `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings`
    `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS FALSE

`a custodial sentence imposed abroad where none would have been imposed in Great Britain` MEANS Sentence WITH
    `the kind of sentence` IS `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings`
    `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS TRUE

`a custodial sentence imposed abroad where one would have been imposed in Great Britain` MEANS Sentence WITH
    `the kind of sentence` IS `a sentence of imprisonment or detention in legal custody as a result of criminal proceedings`
    `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS FALSE

`a mental health detention sentence imposed abroad with the flag set` MEANS Sentence WITH
    `the kind of sentence` IS `a sentence of detention where the provisions mentioned in regulation 2(2)(c)(i) or (d) apply`
    `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS TRUE

`a suspended sentence` MEANS Sentence WITH
    `the kind of sentence` IS `a suspended sentence within the meaning in section 286 of the Sentencing Code`
    `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS FALSE

`a fine` MEANS Sentence WITH
    `the kind of sentence` IS `any other sentence`
    `the sentence was imposed outside Great Britain` IS FALSE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain a sentence of imprisonment or detention would not have been imposed` IS FALSE

-- Regulation 3(2): the three described sentences.
#ASSERT `regulation 3(2): the sentence is a described sentence` `a custodial sentence imposed in Great Britain`
#ASSERT `regulation 3(2): the sentence is a described sentence` `a mental health detention sentence imposed abroad with the flag set`
#ASSERT `regulation 3(2): the sentence is a described sentence` `a suspended sentence`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 3(2): the sentence is a described sentence` `a fine`)
-- Regulation 3(3): a (2)(a) sentence imposed abroad is not described if none would have been imposed in Great Britain.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 3(2): the sentence is a described sentence` `a custodial sentence imposed abroad where none would have been imposed in Great Britain`)
#ASSERT `regulation 3(2): the sentence is a described sentence` `a custodial sentence imposed abroad where one would have been imposed in Great Britain`
-- Regulation 3(3) speaks only of a sentence described in paragraph (2)(a): a (2)(b) sentence imposed abroad stays described.
-- (see the fixture above: kind (b), imposed abroad, flag set.)

§ `Regulation 2(1) with regulation 3: is the state pension not to be paid for the day?`

`imprisoned and not on remand` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
    `the person's custody on the day` IS `imprisoned in Great Britain`
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS FALSE
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS NOTHING

`free and not on remand` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
    `the person's custody on the day` IS `a free person in Great Britain`
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS FALSE
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS NOTHING

`on remand, no sentence yet` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
    `the person's custody on the day` IS `imprisoned in Great Britain`
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS TRUE
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS NOTHING

`on remand, later given a custodial sentence in Great Britain` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
    `the person's custody on the day` IS `imprisoned in Great Britain`
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS TRUE
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS JUST `a custodial sentence imposed in Great Britain`

`on remand, later given a suspended sentence` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
    `the person's custody on the day` IS `imprisoned in Great Britain`
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS TRUE
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS JUST `a suspended sentence`

`on remand, later fined` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
    `the person's custody on the day` IS `imprisoned in Great Britain`
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS TRUE
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS JUST `a fine`

`on remand, later given a custodial sentence abroad that would not have been imposed here` MEANS PrisonStatus WITH
    `the person's custody on the day` IS `imprisoned in Great Britain`
    `the person is remanded in custody for an offence` IS TRUE
    `a sentence later imposed for the offence, if any` IS JUST `a custodial sentence imposed abroad where none would have been imposed in Great Britain`

-- Regulation 2(1): not to be paid for a day on which the person is a prisoner.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `a day in the test period` `imprisoned and not on remand`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `a day in the test period` `free and not on remand`)
-- Regulation 3(1): on remand, regulation 2(1) does not apply ...
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `a day in the test period` `on remand, no sentence yet`)
#ASSERT `regulation 3(1): regulation 2(1) does not apply because the person is remanded in custody` `on remand, no sentence yet`
-- ... unless a described sentence is later imposed for the offence.
#ASSERT `regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `a day in the test period` `on remand, later given a custodial sentence in Great Britain`
#ASSERT `regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `a day in the test period` `on remand, later given a suspended sentence`
-- A sentence that is not described (a fine) leaves regulation 2(1) off.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `a day in the test period` `on remand, later fined`)
-- A (2)(a) sentence abroad that regulation 3(3) excludes leaves regulation 2(1) off.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(1): the state pension is not to be paid for the day` `a day in the test period` `on remand, later given a custodial sentence abroad that would not have been imposed here`)
-- Someone not remanded is not helped by regulation 3(1).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 3(1): regulation 2(1) does not apply because the person is remanded in custody` `imprisoned and not on remand`)

§ `Regulation 2(4)`

-- Text: regulation 13 "shall not have effect" in determining rights to relevant benefits
-- for the purposes of regulation 2. What replaces it the text does not say (fork F7).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 2(4): regulation 13 has effect when determining rights to relevant benefits for regulation 2`)
